```js
createEffect(
  () => fetchData(id()),
  {
    effect: data => renderData(data),
    error: (err, cleanup) => {
      console.error("Fetch failed:", err);
      cleanup();
    },
  },
);
```

The `error` handler catches errors from async computations in the reactive graph. For component-level error UI, use an `Errored` boundary.

