`createStore(fn, seed, options?)` creates a derived store. The function receives a mutable draft and updates it based on reactive sources; the second argument is the seed/backing value, not a memo-style initial value.

```js
const [selected, setSelected] = createStore(draft => {
  const id = selectedId();
  draft[id] = true;
  if (draft._prev != null) delete draft[draft._prev];
  draft._prev = id;
}, {});
```

It is the store analogue of a writable derived signal and supports selector-like patterns without notifying everything.

